    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "A migration inspector finishes his check at Elena's restaurant. He is very impressed. He says there are no illegal workers. They decide to eat at Claude Monet. Let us listen to their conversation in Russian first.",
      "gap": 0.8
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ваш ресторан будет отличным.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы все делаем правильно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Большое спасибо вам.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Вы меня очень удивили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ни одного повара без документов.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я привыкла работать по закону.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Мне было очень приятно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Пойдём в другой ресторан?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Тут есть Клод Моне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отлично, люблю французскую кухню.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "К нам идёт проверка!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Все без документов, вон!",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "Now let us examine the conversation line by line.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ваш ресторан будет отличным.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Your restaurant will be excellent.' Notice how 'your' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'excellent'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Мы все делаем правильно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'We do everything right.' Elena combines 'we' with 'right' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Большое спасибо вам.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Thank you very much.' Elena combines 'big' with 'you' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Вы меня очень удивили.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'You really surprised me.' Here 'to surprise' uses the plural past-tense ending, which also serves for the polite 'you'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Ни одного повара без документов.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Not a single cook without documents.' Russian omits the present-tense verb 'to be', connecting 'not a single' directly with 'documents'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Я привыкла работать по закону.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'I got used to working by the law.' Notice how 'I' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'law'. Then the inspector responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Мне было очень приятно.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'It was very pleasant for me.' the inspector links 'to me' directly with 'was' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Пойдём в другой ресторан?",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Let us go to another restaurant?' the inspector combines 'let's go' with 'restaurant' in a natural Russian turn of phrase.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "leva",
      "t": "Тут есть Клод Моне.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Here is Claude Monet.' Notice how 'here' sets up the clause and leads naturally into 'Monet'.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "anya",
      "t": "Отлично, люблю французскую кухню.",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Excellent, I love French cuisine.' Elena combines 'perfect' with 'kitchen' in a natural Russian turn of phrase. Then Chef Viktor responds.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "К нам идёт проверка!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'An inspection is coming to us!' Chef Viktor links 'us' directly with 'goes' to express the thought clearly.",
      "gap": 0.4
    },
    {
      "v": "dima",
      "t": "Все без документов, вон!",
      "gap": 0.55
    },
    {
      "v": "narrator",
      "t": "'Everyone without documents, get out!' Chef Viktor links 'all' directly with 'without' to express the thought clearly. Now let us listen to the conversation once again.",
      "gap": 0.9
    },
    {
